[
    {
        "text": "Why did people create NFTs? When the world became increasingly digital, people were able to make copies of digital goods easily, such as pirated movies or copied software. Centralized systems were created to reduce those illegal activities. Today, it's extremely hard to download music and movies illegally online, but it remains incredibly easy to make digital copies of many things, and it's hard to prove ownership of digital goods. NFTs allow digital goods to have verifiable scarcity and provable ownership based on blockchain technology. Unlike cryptocurrencies, NFTs are individually unique and are therefore a great solution for representing ownership of unique assets. That's why NFTs are often referred to as crypto collectibles.",
        "start": 240,
        "end": 44540,
        "confidence": 0.98249066,
